              "title": "Laboratory Results",
              "content": "<table class=\"nclex-editor-table\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:12px 0;\"><thead><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:#025287; color:white; font-weight:600; text-align:left;\">Test</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:#025287; color:white; font-weight:600; text-align:left;\">Ethan (Day 3)</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:#025287; color:white; font-weight:600; text-align:left;\">Reference Range</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>Creatine kinase (CK)</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>18,450 U/L</b> (critical high)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">30 – 200 U/L</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>AST</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>168 U/L</b> (high)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">10 – 40 U/L</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>ALT</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>212 U/L</b> (high)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">7 – 40 U/L</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>GGT</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">14 U/L</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">5 – 32 U/L</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>Total bilirubin</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">0.4 mg/dL</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">0.1 – 1.2 mg/dL</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>TSH</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">2.1 mIU/L</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">0.7 – 5.7 mIU/L</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>Potassium</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">4.3 mEq/L</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">3.5 – 5.0 mEq/L</td></tr></tbody></table>"
