          "explanation": "Compared to the 1200 assessment (P 112 beats/min, RR 32 breaths/min, BP 90/62 mm Hg, pulse oximetry 91%, difficult to arouse, pale, diaphoretic), the blood pressure of 118/68 mm Hg is improved (no longer hypotensive), and the client interacting with the adult child at the bedside is improved (previously difficult to arouse). Pale skin tone is not changed (still pale, as before). The pulse oximetry reading of 91% is not changed (identical to the 1200 value). Respirations of 36 breaths/min are worsened (up from 32), showing the client's respiratory status remains a concern even as circulation and mental status are trending in the right direction."
