          "footnote": "Taken from the Maryland Next Gen NCLEX Test Bank Project, University of Maryland School of Nursing: &ldquo;Tuberculosis&rdquo; medical-surgical faculty case study (Elizabeth Mackessy-Lloyd, DNP, RN, CNE, Hood University, September 1, 2022). Available at https://www.nursing.umaryland.edu/mnwc/initiatives/nextgen-nclex/nextgen-nclex-library/ (Faculty Case Studies). Laboratory values shown in SI units.",
          "preamble": "The client is diagnosed with a tuberculosis infection, and orders for new medications are received. The nurse has reviewed the Orders.",
          "explanation": "An N95 respirator protects the nurse from airborne transmission of tuberculosis. Coughing and deep breathing is an important nursing intervention for this client, and the client should be encouraged to wear a face mask around others for at least the first 3 weeks of treatment.<br>While contact tracing would be done for close contacts, the nurse would not reveal the client's identity. The other interventions are not appropriate for this client."
