          "footnote": "Taken from the Maryland Next Gen NCLEX Test Bank Project, University of Maryland School of Nursing: &ldquo;Heart Failure&rdquo; medical-surgical faculty case study (Lisa Seldomridge, PhD, RN, CNE; Jennifer Hart, DNP, FNP-BC; Molly Dale, DNP, FNP-BC; Salisbury University, January 25, 2023). Available at https://www.nursing.umaryland.edu/mnwc/initiatives/nextgen-nclex/nextgen-nclex-library/ (Faculty Case Studies). Laboratory values shown in SI units.",
          "preamble": "",
          "explanation": "The client is having an exacerbation of heart failure and must be taught self-care: daily weights at the same time in the same clothes, limiting dietary sodium, adding potassium-rich foods, and taking medication as prescribed.<br>Increasing fluids would worsen the fluid overload. The usual teaching is to report a gain of 2&ndash;3 lb (1&ndash;1.5 kg) in a day or 5 lb (2.3 kg) in a week. Regular, tolerated activity is encouraged rather than limited."
