          "preamble": "",
          "explanation": "Ascites, a complication of portal hypertension and the low albumin of cirrhosis, increases the abdominal girth, causes bulging flanks and peripheral edema, and can compromise breathing (dyspnea, a low pulse oximetry reading).<br>The deterioration in neurologic status (drowsiness and agitation) results from the increased ammonia level causing hepatic encephalopathy."
