              "title": "Nurses' Notes",
              "content": "<p class=\"nurse-note-row\"><span class=\"nurse-note-time\">1520:</span><span class=\"nurse-note-text\"><b>Emergency department triage note:</b> The client arrives by ambulance with difficulty breathing, sharp chest pain on inspiration, and cough, with onset 2 hours before arrival. Lung sounds diminished bilaterally. Client diaphoretic, tachypneic, using accessory muscles with inspiration. VS: BP 166/103 mm Hg, HR 122 beats/min, RR 36 breaths/min, T 37.2° C, pulse oximetry reading 88% on room air. Client immediately placed in a room. Provider called to bedside for rapid assessment.</span></p>"
