        "leftContent": {
          "tabs": [
            {
              "id": "adm_umd11b",
              "title": "Admission Note",
              "content": "<p>A 39-year-old male client came to the emergency department with shaking chills; maximum temperature reported as 101.2° F (38.4° C). Weight 109.1 kg (240 lb). No known drug allergies. History of end-stage renal disease secondary to heroin nephrotoxicity; on hemodialysis for approximately 7 months.</p><p><b>Current assessment:</b> left upper arm arteriovenous (AV) fistula with a positive thrill and bruit. The AV fistula is red and inflamed. Labs sent.</p>"
            },
            {
              "id": "vs_umd11b",
              "title": "Vital Signs",
              "content": "<table class=\"nclex-editor-table\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:12px 0;\"><thead><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:#025287; color:white; font-weight:600; text-align:left;\"></th><th style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:#025287; color:white; font-weight:600; text-align:left;\">1500</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; background:#025287; color:white; font-weight:600; text-align:left;\">1600</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>T</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">39.2° C (102.6° F)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">40.2° C (104.4° F)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>HR</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">104 beats/min</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">121 beats/min</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>RR</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">18 breaths/min</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">26 breaths/min</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>BP</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">150/92 mm Hg</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">100/64 mm Hg</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>Pulse oximetry reading</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">95% on room air</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">90% on room air</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\"><b>Pain (AV fistula site)</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">6/10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #ccd8e0; padding:8px; min-width:80px; background:white; color:#1e293b;\">8/10</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ],
          "intro": "A 39-year-old male client with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis is seen in the emergency department with fever."
        }
